Implements the OSINT investigation module as a non-breaking complement
to existing functionality:

- New sidebar section 'osint' inserted after queries (preserves all
  existing 13 sections intact).
- Extends DB with 8 new collections: investigations, osintEntities,
  osintRuns, osintFindings, osintRelations, evidence, evidenceEvents,
  sourceCatalog (pre-populated with 14 sources: BrasilAPI suite,
  Receita Federal, Transparência CEIS/CNEP/CEPIM, DataJud, CVM, IBGE,
  RDAP/DNS, manual capture, upload).
- Backward-compatible migration auto-adds new collections to existing
  localStorage DBs without data loss.
- 4-step wizard: identification, objective/hypothesis, legal basis +
  scope, declaration of legitimate purpose (blocking).
- 10-tab workspace per investigation: overview, plan, entities, runs,
  findings, timeline, link map (SVG), evidence vault, report, audit.
- Standardized agent output (status/summary/rawData/confidence/
  limitations) with osintConnectorExecute() abstraction for demo/
  production modes.
- Quick Planner agent generates collection tasks scoped to authorized
  sources only; off-scope attempts auto-blocked and audited.
- Evidence with SHA-256 + hash-chained events (eventHash =
  SHA256(previousHash + eventData)), making tampering detectable.
- Mock connectors for demo mode with visible 'Demonstração' labeling;
  production mode requires backend.
- 18-section investigative report (printable PDF) with cover,
  methodology, sources, entities, timeline, findings, evidence,
  limitations, integrity manifesto, verification code, document hash.
- 5-level finding classification (raw → indicio → achado →
  corroborated → human conclusion) with distinct colors/icons.
- escapeHTML() applied to all user-rendered values; sensitive
  identifiers logged only as masked + 12-char fingerprint.
- OSINT-specific audit actions (criacao_investigacao, aprovacao_escopo,
  execucao_coleta, falha_coleta, inclusao_evidencia, validacao,
  exclusao_logica, geracao_relatorio).
- Smoke-tested: 20/20 integration checks pass, JS syntax validated.

